{
  "description": "A worn controller in the fit tool (tools/probe/xr_tool.h, StickCal): the left stick comes to rest off centre (0.58 up and to the right) right after A and stays there; under the 1.5.1 rule (any stick past half its travel is a key) that moved the upper-right corner by itself. Now its rest point is learned (re-centred) and both sticks go through Microsoft's scaled radial dead zones, so the drift moves nothing, the right stick works as in e2e_fov_tool_pad, and a full push of the drifted left stick (frame 300) still maps to 'left' from its new centre. Expected: the right stick's edits and the left push, and no corner moved by the drift.",
